            <p>This analysis examines 41,729 user reviews across the five leading generative AI mobile applications. While the dataset was designed for 50,000 reviews, 41,729 were successfully retrieved and processed. The analysis reveals significant differentiation in user satisfaction, complaint patterns, and sentiment-rating alignment.</p>

            <div class="exec-summary">
                <h3>Key Strategic Takeaways</h3>
                <div class="key-takeaways">
                    <div class="takeaway">
                        <h4>1. Microsoft Copilot Leads in Satisfaction</h4>
                        <p>Copilot achieves the highest average star rating (4.24) and sentiment polarity (0.49), with 68% 5-star reviews. Its strongest differentiator is the lowest sentiment-rating mismatch rate (3.6%), indicating genuine positive sentiment.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="takeaway">
                        <h4>2. Perplexity Faces Trust Issues</h4>
                        <p>Despite having the most 1-star reviews (31%), Perplexity shows the highest sentiment-rating mismatch (7.7%), suggesting sarcasm and complex emotions that simple star ratings don't capture. Its accuracy complaints are also highest (6.4%).</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="takeaway">
                        <h4>3. Bugs/Performance Resonates Most</h4>
                        <p>Bugs/Performance complaints generate 4x more "helpful" votes than other themes, indicating these issues strongly influence user retention. Perplexity's bug-related reviews get 27.5 thumbs-up average vs 2.1 for ChatGPT.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="kpi-grid">
